---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="CivicNavigator — Means+Measures" description="Civic navigation and mutual aid: understand institutional paperwork, organize a useful record, and find practical next steps and human support.">
  <section class="section">
    <p class="eyebrow">CivicNavigator · Means+Measures</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title">Understand what affects you. Find a way forward.</h1>
    <div class="measure">
      <p>CivicNavigator is a Means+Measures product and service in development for civic navigation and mutual aid. It brings plain-language document help, practical resource navigation, and human support into the same process.</p>
      <p>A letter, form, or institutional decision can leave you with more questions than answers. CivicNavigator is being built to help you understand what you received, organize the relevant record, and carry useful information into your next interaction.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--compact">
    <div class="grid">
      <section><h2 class="card-title">Understand the paperwork</h2><p>Housing notices, benefits correspondence, insurance forms, court papers, and school or government documents—explained in everyday language.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="card-title">Keep a useful record</h2><p>Bring the documents, questions, and next steps together so you can return to the process without starting over.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="card-title">Find practical routes</h2><p>Connect your situation to resources and people who can help, including services across the Kansas City bi-state metro.</p></section>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--compact">
    <div class="measure">
      <h2>Down through systems. Up through people.</h2>
      <p>CivicNavigator grows from the original BJL13 civic-assistance application into Means+Measures’ document-forward infrastructure work. The direction remains personal agency, understandable processes, control over personal information, and support for the people already doing the work.</p>
      <h2>While we build</h2>
      <p>The application is not yet available as a public service. You can use the <a href="/kc">Kansas City resource directory</a> now, or <a href="/contact">contact Means+Measures</a> about CivicNavigator and potential collaboration.</p>
      <p><a href="/systems">Explore the Means+Measures systems</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
